---
import SolutionPage from '../../layouts/SolutionPage.astro';
---

<SolutionPage
  title="Substance Use & Dependency"
  parent="Mitigate"
  oneliner="Alcohol, nicotine, and habitual stimulant use are often misread as personal failures — they're behavioral patterns with biological drivers."
  slug="substance-use"
>

  <!-- ── Why this matters ── -->
  <h2>Why this is harder than willpower</h2>
  <p>
    Alcohol and nicotine dependence are not character flaws. Both substances physically
    restructure the brain's reward circuitry — dopamine pathways, GABA and glutamate balance,
    opioid receptor sensitivity. With repeated use, the brain recalibrates its baseline so that
    normal life feels flat without the substance. That is not weakness; it is neurobiology.
    Treating it like a motivation problem is why most willpower-only attempts fail within days.
  </p>
  <p>
    For men 35–60, the long arc matters most. A decade of two-to-four drinks nightly doesn't
    just affect the liver — it progressively degrades hippocampal volume, disrupts growth
    hormone pulsatility, inflames the gut lining, and fractures sleep architecture in ways that
    compound every other health problem. The same decade of daily nicotine quietly accelerates
    cerebrovascular disease and systemic inflammation. These are slow, largely silent costs that
    show up clearly on a decade-level health trajectory.
  </p>
  <p>
    Crucially, reduction is medically meaningful even when full cessation feels out of reach.
    Research consistently shows that cutting consumption in half — not to zero, but by 50% —
    over a sustained period preserves significant cognitive function, reduces cancer risk, and
    partially reverses cardiovascular damage. The goal is not perfection. The goal is a better
    trajectory. That framing makes this work sustainable.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Our approach ── -->
  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Honest Inventory</h3>
      <p>Structured self-assessment covering frequency, quantity, context, and function — no judgment, just data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Upstream Root Causes</h3>
      <p>Most habitual use is a coping mechanism for stress, poor sleep, or social isolation. Address those first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Replacement Protocol</h3>
      <p>Behavioral substitutions that meet the same need — relaxation, social bonding, stimulation — without the metabolic cost.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Referral Pathway</h3>
      <p>We maintain relationships with evidence-based addiction specialists and telehealth MAT providers for individuals who need more support.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Free supportive resources — trust frame ── -->
  <div class="trust-note">
    <p>
      We don't only sell solutions. Here are the proven free programs that have helped tens of millions
      reduce or eliminate alcohol — independent of My4MLife.
    </p>
    <p class="trust-disclaimer">
      These resources have helped millions. Some require a clinician (Sinclair Method); most are free,
      peer-led, or self-guided. We list them because they work — not because we get a kickback.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Alcohol: self-directed / behavioral ── -->
  <h2>Free supportive resources — alcohol</h2>
  <h3 class="resource-category">Self-directed &amp; behavioral</h3>
  <div class="resource-grid">

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">SMART Recovery</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Secular · CBT-based</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Cognitive behavioral approach to addiction recovery. Online and in-person meetings worldwide, no steps required.</p>
      <a href="https://www.smartrecovery.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">The Sinclair Method (TSM)</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Clinician-guided</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Naltrexone taken before drinking triggers "pharmacological extinction" — gradually reducing the reward of alcohol over weeks. Requires a prescribing clinician. Evidence base is strong.</p>
      <a href="https://www.thesinclairmethod.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Allen Carr's Easy Way to Stop Drinking</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Self-guided · Book</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Cognitive reframing approach that dismantles the psychological dependency. Available at most public libraries at no cost.</p>
      <a href="https://www.allencarr.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Quit Lit Reading List</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Self-guided · Books</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">
        Three evidence-informed books worth your time:
        <em>This Naked Mind</em> (Annie Grace),
        <em>Drink? The New Science of Alcohol and Your Health</em> (David Nutt),
        <em>Sober Curious</em> (Ruby Warrington).
        All available via library or purchase.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Recovery Dharma</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Mindfulness-based · Peer</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Buddhist-informed peer recovery community. Free meetings in person and online. No religious requirement — emphasizes meditation and community.</p>
      <a href="https://www.recoverydharma.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Refuge Recovery</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Mindfulness-based · Peer</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Mindfulness-based recovery community. Free meetings, secular framework grounded in Buddhist principles of reducing suffering.</p>
      <a href="https://www.refugerecovery.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

  <h3 class="resource-category">12-Step (for those who want it)</h3>
  <div class="resource-grid">

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">AA — Alcoholics Anonymous</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Fellowship-based · Free</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Free, peer-led fellowship meetings worldwide. Decades of documented effectiveness for individuals who resonate with the fellowship model.</p>
      <a href="https://www.aa.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Al-Anon</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">For family &amp; friends</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Support for family members and friends of someone struggling with alcohol — because the people around the drinker need support too.</p>
      <a href="https://al-anon.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

  <h3 class="resource-category">Apps &amp; tools</h3>
  <div class="resource-grid">

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Sunnyside</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Moderation · App</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Habit-tracking app built for people who want to drink less, not necessarily quit. Goal-setting, tracking, and accountability nudges.</p>
      <a href="https://www.sunnyside.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Reframe</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Neuroscience · App</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Neuroscience-backed habit-change app with daily check-ins, education modules, and a supportive peer community.</p>
      <a href="https://www.reframeapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">I Am Sober</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Sobriety counter · Community</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Sobriety counter, daily pledge, milestone milestones, and a peer community. Simple, low-friction, available on iOS and Android.</p>
      <a href="https://iamsober.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

  <h3 class="resource-category">Crisis &amp; immediate support</h3>
  <div class="resource-grid">

    <div class="resource-card resource-card--highlight">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">SAMHSA National Helpline</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">24/7 · Free · Confidential</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">
        <strong>1-800-662-HELP (4357)</strong> — Free, confidential treatment referral and information service.
        Available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, in English and Spanish. No insurance required.
      </p>
      <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/find-help/national-helpline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">AUDIT Self-Screen</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Self-assessment · Free</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">The Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test — 10 validated questions developed by the WHO. Gives you an objective score to bring to a clinician or use as a baseline.</p>
      <a href="https://auditscreen.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Take the AUDIT →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ── Smoking + vaping resources ── -->
  <h2>Free supportive resources — smoking &amp; vaping</h2>
  <div class="resource-grid">

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">truth Initiative</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Education · Tools</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Research-backed quit resources, text-to-quit programs, and a focus on youth and young-adult cessation. Strong digital tools.</p>
      <a href="https://truthinitiative.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">CDC — How to Quit Smoking</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Government resource · Free</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Step-by-step quit guide, tips for managing cravings, and links to local and national support programs. No cost.</p>
      <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/tobacco/quit_smoking/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">Nicotine Anonymous (NicA)</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">12-step · Peer · Free</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Fellowship-based program specifically for nicotine dependency. Free meetings online and in person. Modeled on the AA framework.</p>
      <a href="https://nicotine-anonymous.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-link">Visit →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card resource-card--highlight">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">State Quit Lines</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">Phone coaching · Free</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">
        <strong>1-800-QUIT-NOW (1-800-784-8669)</strong> — Free telephone coaching from trained quit specialists.
        Available in every US state. Call any time to connect with your state's program.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-card">
      <div class="resource-header">
        <span class="resource-name">NRT — Nicotine Replacement Therapy</span>
        <span class="resource-tag">OTC + Rx options</span>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-desc">Patches, gum, lozenges, and inhalers are available OTC and have a solid evidence base. Prescription options (varenicline, bupropion) are stronger — discuss with a clinician. Combining NRT with behavioral support significantly increases success rates.</p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ── How My4MLife supports the journey ── -->
  <h2>How My4MLife supports your reduction journey</h2>
  <p>
    We won't replace these programs — but we can support the physiological piece while you work them.
    Recovery is not just behavioral; the body needs to heal alongside the habit change.
  </p>
  <div class="support-bullets">
    <div class="support-item">
      <span class="support-product">Biome-AF</span>
      <span class="support-desc">Gut healing after years of alcohol-driven intestinal inflammation. Alcohol degrades the gut lining; this formula supports repair.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="support-item">
      <span class="support-product">NeuroBridge</span>
      <span class="support-desc">Methylated B-complex. Alcohol depletes B-vitamins — especially B12 and folate — which are essential for neurotransmitter synthesis during early recovery.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="support-item">
      <span class="support-product">SleepRestore</span>
      <span class="support-desc">Sleep architecture is significantly disrupted during the first 30–90 days of cessation. This stack supports natural sleep cycling while your brain recalibrates.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="consult-cta">
    <a href="/consult">Schedule a comprehensive 4M consult</a> if you want to discuss naltrexone,
    varenicline, or other prescription support options as part of your reduction plan.
  </p>

</SolutionPage>

<style>
/* ── Trust note ── */
.trust-note {
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
}
.trust-note p { margin: 0; }
.trust-note p + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
.trust-disclaimer {
  font-size: 0.88rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
  font-style: italic;
}

/* ── Resource category heading ── */
.resource-category {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-light);
  margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem;
}

/* ── Resource grid ── */
.resource-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

/* ── Resource card ── */
.resource-card {
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.45rem;
}
.resource-card--highlight {
  border-color: rgba(0,184,148,0.45);
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.04);
}
.resource-header {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}
.resource-name {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--primary);
}
.resource-tag {
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--accent);
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.1);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,184,148,0.3);
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.resource-desc {
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 0;
}
.resource-link {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--accent);
  text-decoration: none;
  margin-top: auto;
  padding-top: 0.35rem;
}
.resource-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

/* ── Support bullets (My4MLife physiological support) ── */
.support-bullets {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  margin: 1.25rem 0;
}
.support-item {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  align-items: baseline;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  font-size: 0.9rem;
}
.support-product {
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--primary);
  white-space: nowrap;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.support-desc {
  color: var(--text-light);
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* ── Consult CTA ── */
.consult-cta {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
}
.consult-cta a {
  color: var(--accent);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.consult-cta a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
